# seccomp-tighten.list — OpenWrt container seccomp floor: removal delta
#
# Syscalls removed from the allow-list that survives resolving seccomp-base.json
# for the target arch with an EMPTY capability set. One token per line; the rest
# of the line is the justification. Blank lines and '#' comments are ignored.
# A token may be a single syscall name or a Podman cap-group name prefixed with
# '@' (e.g. @CAP_SYS_ADMIN) to drop every name a cap-group would have allowed.
#
# Principle: the floor runs with zero caps, all namespaces, noNewPrivileges and a
# read-only root. Podman's default profile leans on capabilities for the real
# boundary and therefore leaves a number of powerful syscalls in the
# unconditional ALLOW group. App/runtime containers do not need them, so we drop
# them. Each removed syscall already returns ENOSYS/EPERM by defaultAction; the
# only behavioural change for a well-behaved app is none. Anything an ordinary
# Go/C/musl app, a shell, or a process supervisor needs is deliberately KEPT
# (futex*, epoll*, clock_gettime*, openat*, read/write*, mmap/mprotect,
# clone/clone3, the *xattr family, prctl, the socket family, etc.).

## --- keyring family: credential theft / kernel keyring abuse, never used by apps
add_key             kernel keyring write; not needed by app containers
request_key         kernel keyring lookup; not needed by app containers
keyctl              kernel keyring control; classic container-escape surface

## --- mount / filesystem-namespace manipulation: with user-ns these widen escape surface
mount               new mounts inside the container are a floor violation; opt back in via CONTAINER_SECCOMP_ALLOW
umount              unmounting host/overlay mounts; not needed by apps
umount2             unmounting host/overlay mounts; not needed by apps
mount_setattr       remount/propagation changes; mount-namespace tampering
move_mount          new-mount-API relocate; mount-namespace tampering
open_tree           new-mount-API tree clone; mount-namespace tampering
fsopen              new-mount-API fs context create
fsconfig            new-mount-API fs context configure
fsmount             new-mount-API attach
fspick              new-mount-API pick
pivot_root          swap the root mount; only a runtime/init-of-host needs it, not the payload
chroot              change root dir; not needed by app payloads (ENOSYS already w/o CAP_SYS_CHROOT, dropped to be explicit)

## --- ptrace / cross-process inspection: defeats process isolation inside the ns
ptrace              trace/peek/poke other processes; debugger-only, escape aid
process_vm_readv    read another process's memory
process_vm_writev   write another process's memory
kcmp                compare kernel resources of two processes; info-leak/ASLR oracle
process_madvise     advise on another process's memory; cross-process reach

## --- BPF / perf / tracing: kernel attack surface, needs privilege to be useful anyway
bpf                 load eBPF; major kernel attack surface
perf_event_open     perf subsystem; kernel info-leak/attack surface

## --- module / kernel-image / power: host-level operations a container must never do
init_module         load kernel module
finit_module        load kernel module (fd form)
delete_module       unload kernel module
query_module        legacy module query
kexec_load          load a new kernel
kexec_file_load     load a new kernel (fd form)
reboot              reboot/halt/power-off the host

## --- time/clock and host identity: host-global state, not container-scoped
clock_settime       set the system clock (host-global; container has no business)
clock_settime64     set the system clock (32-bit time_t variant)
clock_adjtime       slew/step the system clock
clock_adjtime64     slew/step the system clock (32-bit time_t variant)
adjtimex            adjust kernel clock parameters
settimeofday        set wall-clock time
stime               set wall-clock time (legacy)
sethostname         change host name (uts is namespaced, but app payloads don't need it)
setdomainname       change NIS domain name

## --- swap / accounting / quota / misc admin
swapon              enable swap; host storage admin
swapoff             disable swap; host storage admin
acct                BSD process accounting; host-global
quotactl            disk quota control; host storage admin
quotactl_fd         disk quota control (fd form)
nfsservctl          ancient NFS server control
vhangup            virtually hang up the controlling tty; host tty admin
lookup_dcookie      legacy oprofile dcookie lookup
ustat               obsolete fs stats; attack surface, no callers
sysfs               obsolete fs-type enumeration; no modern callers

## --- raw I/O / port / descriptor-table poking
ioperm              grant raw I/O port access (x86); hardware reach
iopl                raise I/O privilege level (x86); hardware reach
pciconfig_read      raw PCI config read
pciconfig_write     raw PCI config write
pciconfig_iobase    raw PCI io base query
pidfd_getfd         steal an fd from another process; sandbox-bypass primitive

## --- namespace / privilege boundary widening from inside
unshare             create new namespaces inside the container; do not let payloads re-namespace
setns               enter another namespace; needs an external fd, but deny by floor
open_by_handle_at   resolve a file handle, bypassing path-based confinement (the classic Shocker escape)
name_to_handle_at   produce the handle open_by_handle_at consumes; dropped as a pair

## --- W^X / shadow-stack helpers that fight the MDWE floor
map_shadow_stack    CET shadow-stack mapping; not needed and interacts with MDWE

## --- fanotify: filesystem-wide watch / permission events (in the unconditional
##     ALLOW group of the base; cap-gated in practice, never used by app payloads)
fanotify_init       global filesystem watch/permission events
fanotify_mark       add fanotify marks across mounts; pairs with fanotify_init

## --- x86 LDT: recurring local-privilege-escalation surface (arch-conditional)
modify_ldt          modify the per-process LDT; recurring x86 LPE surface (CVE-2017-17053 et al)

## --- s390 raw hardware reach (arch-conditional; absent on other targets)
s390_pci_mmio_read  raw PCI MMIO read (s390); hardware reach, like pciconfig_*/iopl
s390_pci_mmio_write raw PCI MMIO write (s390); hardware reach
s390_runtime_instr  s390 CPU runtime-instrumentation; privileged hardware feature

# ============================================================================
# Second-tier floor (2026-06-10): cut everything beyond a hello-world app /
# unprivileged-port listener. The kept set is I/O, the socket family, epoll/
# poll/select, mmap/munmap/mremap/madvise, futex*, signals, clock/time, the
# identity getters, clone/clone3 (threads), kill/tkill/tgkill, and the common
# file ops (open/read/write/symlink/mkdir/rename/unlink/truncate). Everything
# below returns the profile default (EPERM); a container that needs one opts
# back in via CONTAINER_SECCOMP_ALLOW.

## --- exec family: a payload does not re-exec itself; a supervisor opts in
execve              replace the process image; not a floor need
execveat            replace the process image (fd form)

## --- W^X mapping: granted by the linker/init phase bases for loader RELRO and
##     runtime init then revoked at main, so it need not sit in the base; W^X is
##     enforced by MDWE regardless. JIT/dlopen runtimes opt back in.
mprotect            change page protections; phase-provided for startup, denied to the workload
pkey_mprotect       protection-key mprotect variant; opt in
pkey_alloc          allocate a protection key; opt in
pkey_free           free a protection key; opt in

## --- subprocess creation: clone/clone3 (threads) are kept; spawning a separate
##     process (shelling out) is opt-in
fork                spawn a child process; opt in
vfork               spawn a child process (shared mm); opt in

## --- SysV IPC: not used by network apps
shmget              SysV shared-memory get
shmat               SysV shared-memory attach
shmdt               SysV shared-memory detach
shmctl              SysV shared-memory control
semget              SysV semaphore get
semop               SysV semaphore op
semctl              SysV semaphore control
semtimedop          SysV semaphore timed op
semtimedop_time64   SysV semaphore timed op (32-bit time_t)
msgget              SysV message-queue get
msgsnd              SysV message send
msgrcv              SysV message receive
msgctl              SysV message-queue control
ipc                 multiplexed SysV IPC entry (32-bit)

## --- POSIX message queues
mq_open             open a POSIX mqueue
mq_unlink           remove a POSIX mqueue
mq_timedsend        send to a POSIX mqueue
mq_timedsend_time64 send to a POSIX mqueue (32-bit time_t)
mq_timedreceive     receive from a POSIX mqueue
mq_timedreceive_time64 receive from a POSIX mqueue (32-bit time_t)
mq_notify           request mqueue notification
mq_getsetattr       get/set mqueue attributes

## --- io_uring: large asynchronous-I/O attack surface; opt in
io_uring_setup      create an io_uring instance
io_uring_enter      submit/complete io_uring requests
io_uring_register   register io_uring resources
io_setup            create an AIO context
io_submit           submit AIO requests
io_getevents        reap AIO completions
io_cancel           cancel an AIO request
io_destroy          destroy an AIO context
io_pgetevents       reap AIO completions (signal mask)
io_pgetevents_time64 reap AIO completions (32-bit time_t)

## --- extended attributes: a read-only-root app sets no xattrs
setxattr            set an extended attribute
lsetxattr           set an xattr (no-follow)
fsetxattr           set an xattr (fd)
getxattr            read an extended attribute
lgetxattr           read an xattr (no-follow)
fgetxattr           read an xattr (fd)
listxattr           list extended attributes
llistxattr          list xattrs (no-follow)
flistxattr          list xattrs (fd)
removexattr         remove an extended attribute
lremovexattr        remove an xattr (no-follow)
fremovexattr        remove an xattr (fd)

## --- ownership / mode mutation: a read-only-root app changes no permissions
chmod               change file mode
fchmod              change file mode (fd)
fchmodat            change file mode (at)
fchmodat2           change file mode (at, flags)
chown               change owner
chown32             change owner (32-bit ids)
fchown              change owner (fd)
fchown32            change owner (fd, 32-bit ids)
lchown              change owner (no-follow)
lchown32            change owner (no-follow, 32-bit ids)
fchownat            change owner (at)

## --- device-node and hard-link creation: not a floor need (symlink/mkdir/
##     rename/unlink/truncate are kept)
mknod               create a device/special node
mknodat             create a device/special node (at)
link                create a hard link
linkat              create a hard link (at)

## --- NUMA / memory-policy: not needed by app payloads
mbind               set NUMA memory policy for a range
set_mempolicy       set the process NUMA policy
get_mempolicy       query the NUMA policy
migrate_pages       migrate pages between NUMA nodes
move_pages          move pages to NUMA nodes

## --- exploit / anti-hardening primitives
userfaultfd         userspace page-fault handling; classic exploit primitive
memfd_create        anonymous in-memory file; fileless-payload staging, opt in
memfd_secret        secret memory region; uncommon, opt in
personality         change execution domain (can disable ASLR)
uselib              load a shared library the ancient way; dead, attack surface

## --- inotify: filesystem watching (config reload); a listener does not need it
inotify_init        create an inotify instance
inotify_init1       create an inotify instance (flags)
inotify_add_watch   add an inotify watch
inotify_rm_watch    remove an inotify watch

## --- memory-lock DoS (mlock/munlock kept; lock-everything is the DoS)
mlockall            lock all current/future pages
munlockall          unlock all pages

## --- scheduling / priority setters (the getters are kept; sched_setaffinity is
##     kept for runtimes that pin threads)
setpriority         raise/lower nice value
nice                raise/lower nice value (legacy)
ioprio_set          set I/O scheduling priority
sched_setscheduler  change scheduling policy
sched_setparam      change scheduling parameters
sched_setattr       change scheduling attributes

## --- legacy / info-leak / dead aliases
syslog              read the kernel log ring buffer; info leak
vm86                enter v8086 mode (x86 legacy)
vm86old             enter v8086 mode (x86 legacy)
sgetmask            get the signal mask (obsolete)
ssetmask            set the signal mask (obsolete)
bdflush             obsolete buffer-dirty flush control
oldolduname         obsolete uname variant
oldstat             obsolete stat variant
oldlstat            obsolete lstat variant
oldfstat            obsolete fstat variant
olduname            obsolete uname variant

## --- pidfd cross-process reach
pidfd_open          obtain a pidfd for another process
pidfd_send_signal   signal another process via pidfd
process_mrelease    release the memory of a dying process

## --- init-phase-provided: in linker_base/init_base, so granted during loading/
##     init and revoked at main; these are startup/init concerns not re-issued by
##     the workload at runtime, so they need not sit in the base (like mprotect).
prctl               process-control setup (name/dumpable/MDWE) at init; not a runtime workload call
prlimit64           resource limits read at init; apps rarely change limits at runtime
set_tid_address     clear-child-tid registered once for the main thread at start
set_robust_list     robust-futex list; glibc treats failure as best-effort (loses only robust-mutex auto-cleanup)
sched_getscheduler  scheduling-policy query at init; not a runtime call
